From 550f95ec31ef5951f4de727b45ba5a78a147e184 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:00:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] draw the contents of PowerClip frames

An object whose loda record has argument 0x1f45 is a PowerClip frame.
The argument's first word is the spnd id of the vect holding the artwork
clipped into the frame. libcdr parsed that vect into m_vects but never
drew it, so all PowerClipped artwork went missing.

readLoda now passes the id to the new collectPowerClip. collectLevel
records the box each vect was drawn in (m_vectBoxes). When the frame's
path is flushed, the content collector emits, right after the frame, a
graphic object of MIME type image/svg+xml over the contents' box. It is
a small SVG whose clipPath is the frame's outline, wrapped around the
vect's own SVG, so the contents are clipped to the frame the way
CorelDRAW draws them, in any consumer that renders SVG images.
